Package: edemint-ai
Version: 0.1
Maintainer: Edemint <hello@edemint.invalid>
Homepage: https://example.invalid/edemint
Architecture: all
Depends: @DEPS@
Description: Edemint AI assistant — pluggable LLM helper (off by default)
 The Edemint AI assistant is a thin shell helper that routes prompts to a
 user-selected backend: cloud LLM (Claude / OpenAI / Gemini, with API keys
 stored in gnome-keyring), local LLM (ollama, no model bundled by default),
 or NPU vision (Pi AI HAT+ / Hailo, Pi 5 only). The package ships disabled;
 `edemint-ai enable` opts in. A local-only switch refuses cloud backends
 for users who want zero egress.
